  '[topic how-it-works] How it works\n1. Preview: Browse all 1,000 Founding Passes, heart your favourites, and join the waitlist. Minting hasn’t started, and anyone can try the app with a free Sneaker.\n2. Early access: On Saturday 21 November, the game starts over for the Founding Pass. From then, only founders can play, and Sneakers and STRIDE from before don’t carry over.\n3. Waitlist window: For 48 hours, people who joined the waitlist before it opened mint first. One free pass each.\n4. Open mint: Then anyone can mint what’s left, until all 1,000 are minted.\n5. The app: Sign in to the StrideMon app with the wallet that holds your pass. You get a Founder Sneaker in your pass’s design, and your first walk laces both.\n6. Open to all: When all 1,000 are minted, or on the last date in the schedule, anyone can play with a free Sneaker. No new passes, ever.\n\n[topic before-you-start] Before you start\n- An Android phone. The app is Android only for now. iOS comes later.\n- MetaMask, a free wallet app. Your wallet is your StrideMon account.\n- Monad Testnet turned on in MetaMask. It’s free, and it takes one tap below on a laptop.\n- An email address, to check it’s you when you mint.\n- The StrideMon app, once you’ve minted.\nYou don’t need any money. Minting is free, and there’s no gas to pay: StrideMon pays it.\n\n[topic install-metamask] Guide: Install MetaMask\nMetaMask is a free wallet app. It holds your pass and your Sneaker, and it’s how you sign in.\n1. On your Android phone, open Google Play and install MetaMask (by Consensys). On a laptop, add the MetaMask extension to Chrome, Brave, Firefox or Edge.\n2. Open it and tap Create a new wallet. Choose a password.\n3. Write the Secret Recovery Phrase (12 words) on paper and keep it somewhere safe. It’s the only way back into your wallet if you lose your phone.\nNever share your Secret Recovery Phrase. StrideMon will never ask for it, and nobody honest will.\nLink: Get MetaMask (https://metamask.io/download/)\n\n[topic add-monad-testnet] Guide: Add Monad Testnet\nStrideMon runs on Monad Testnet, a test network. Adding it is free, and the app needs it.\n1. On a laptop with MetaMask, or in MetaMask’s own browser on your phone: tap Add Monad Testnet below, then approve in MetaMask.\n2. Or open MetaMask, tap the network menu at the top, then Add a custom network, and type the details below.\n3. Turn it on before you connect to StrideMon. A wallet only shares your account for networks it has turned on.\nThe details, to add by hand: Network name Monad Testnet; RPC URL https://testnet-rpc.monad.xyz; Chain ID 10143; Currency MON; Explorer https://testnet.monadvision.com.\n\n[topic get-ready] Guide: Get ready: check your email and sign in\nDo this before you mint, so minting is one tap when the time comes.\n1. Open stridemon.xyz/pass. Get ready shows near the top from the day before minting opens.\n2. Type your email and tap Send code. If a robot check shows, let it finish.\n3. Type the 6-digit code from our email. It works for 10 minutes. Look in spam if it isn’t in your inbox.\n4. Tap Connect wallet and pick MetaMask. On a phone, MetaMask opens: approve, then come back.\n5. Tap Sign in and approve the message in MetaMask. It’s free and sends nothing.\nUse the wallet you’ll use in the app. The email check lasts 6 hours, so do it on the day.\nLink: Open Get ready (https://stridemon.xyz/pass#get-ready)\n\n[topic mint] Guide: Mint your pass\n1. Pick a pass: browse the gallery, take the quiz, or tap Surprise me. Tap a pass to open it.\n2. Tap Mint. If you skipped Get ready, its two steps show first.\n3. Wait a few seconds while it mints on Monad. Keep the page open.\n4. Your pass turns over with your founder number. It’s yours.\nSomeone took it a moment before you? Nothing is minted for you, and you see three similar passes nobody has yet. One tap mints one.\n\n[topic get-the-app] Guide: Get the app\n1. On your Android phone, tap Get the app after your mint, or the link below. It downloads the StrideMon app.\n2. Open the downloaded file. If Android asks, allow installs from your browser.\n3. Open StrideMon.\nAndroid may say the app isn’t from Google Play. That’s expected for this test build.\nLink: Download the app (https://expo.dev/artifacts/eas/Aa0J7FXKPHyaKSGL-74nW66qSugLVcvhOMLyRrGL2iY.apk)\n\n[topic sign-in-app] Guide: Sign in with the same wallet\nThe app knows you’re a founder by the wallet that holds your pass.\n1. In the app, tap Connect wallet and pick MetaMask.\n2. In MetaMask, pick the account that holds your pass, with Monad Testnet turned on, and approve.\n3. Back in the app, tap Sign to verify it’s you, and approve the message. It’s free.\n4. The app finds your pass and mints your Founder Sneaker. It takes a few seconds.\nThe app shows the address you signed in with. If it says you have no pass, you’re probably on another account: sign out and sign in with the one you minted with.\n\n[topic first-walk] Guide: Your first walk\n1. On Home, tap Start a run. Allow location, so the app can count your minutes.\n2. Walk or run. Minutes faster than 20 km/h don’t count, so no driving.\n3. Tap Stop. Your STRIDE arrives on Monad a few seconds later.\n4. Your first walk laces your pass and your Founder Sneaker. Both pictures change.\n\n[topic whats-free] What’s free?\nEverything. The pass, the Founder Sneaker and the app are free. StrideMon pays the gas, and gives new players a little test MON. You never pay anything.\n\n[topic pass-or-sneaker] Is the Founding Pass my Sneaker?\nNo, they’re two things. The pass is your membership card: you mint it on the website, and it shows you’re a founder. You don’t walk with it.\nThe Founder Sneaker is the shoe you walk with. The app gives it to you, drawn in your pass’s design, when you sign in with the wallet that holds the pass. Neither can be sent or sold.\nLink: Sign in with the same wallet (topic sign-in-app)\n\n[topic two-numbers] Why does my pass have two numbers?\nThe pass number, like #0137, is the design: which of the 1,000 you picked. Every design exists once.\nThe founder number, like Founder 42, is the order you minted in: you were the 42nd founder to mint.\n\n[topic play-before-pass] Can I play the app before I have a pass?\nUntil early access starts on Saturday 21 November, yes: anyone can try it with a free Sneaker. That’s a test period.\nWhen early access starts, the game starts over. Sneakers and STRIDE from the test period don’t carry over, and only founders can play. Nobody has a pass until the waitlist window opens, so the app waits until then.\nWhen all 1,000 are minted, or on the last date in the schedule, anyone can play again with a free Sneaker.\nLink: See the Founding Passes (https://stridemon.xyz/pass)\n\n[topic cant-be-sent-or-sold] What does “can’t be sent or sold” mean?\nYour pass and your Founder Sneaker stay in the wallet you minted with. Nobody can buy them, and you can’t move them to another wallet yourself.\nThe pass isn’t a token and never turns into one. If you lose that wallet, support can move both for you.\nLink: Lost your wallet? (topic lost-wallet)\n\n[topic why-email] Why do you need my email?\nTo keep it to one pass per person, and so you can prove the pass is yours if you lose your wallet.\nWe send a code when you check your email, and one email when the waitlist window opens. Nothing else.\nLink: Privacy policy (https://stridemon.xyz/privacy)\n\n[topic which-wallet] Which wallet should I use?\nThe one you’ll use in the app. The app knows you’re a founder by the wallet that holds your pass. MetaMask works on Android and as a laptop extension.\nLink: Install MetaMask (topic install-metamask)\n\n[topic stride-value] Is STRIDE worth money?\nNo. STRIDE is a test token on Monad Testnet, and it has no monetary value. You earn it by walking and spend it on your Sneaker.\n\n[topic laced] What does “laced” mean?\nYour first walk in the app laces your pass and your Founder Sneaker: the laces go in, and the card says LACED. It’s only for looks.\n\n[topic after-all-minted] What happens after all 1,000 are minted?\nNo new passes, ever. StrideMon opens to everyone with a free normal Sneaker. If they aren’t all minted, it opens on the last date in the schedule anyway. Founders keep their pass and Founder Sneaker.\n\n[topic code-not-arriving] Your email: The code didn’t arrive.\nLook in spam and promotions for an email from hello@stridemon.xyz. It can take a minute.\nCheck your email for a typo. You can ask for a new code after a minute, and only the newest code works.\nLink: Write to us (topic contact)\n\n[topic wrong-code] Your email: The code doesn’t work.\nUse the code in the newest email: a new code stops the old one working.\nA code works for 10 minutes and 5 tries. After that, ask for a new one and type it carefully.\n\n[topic robot-check] Your email: The robot check fails or won’t load.\nIt’s Cloudflare Turnstile, and it keeps bots from using up the mint. Wait for it to reload, then try again.\nIf it never shows, a content blocker may be stopping it. Allow stridemon.xyz or try another browser, then reload the page.\n\n[topic check-ran-out] Your email: “Your email check ran out” or “Your sign-in ended”.\nAn email check lasts 6 hours. Check your email again: it takes a minute.\nA sign-in also ends after a while. Sign in with your wallet again. It’s free.\n\n[topic no-wallet] Your wallet: I don’t have a wallet, or none is connected.\nInstall MetaMask first. It’s free and takes a few minutes. Then tap Connect wallet and pick it.\nWhen your wallet asks to add or switch to Monad Testnet, say yes. It’s free.\nLink: Install MetaMask (topic install-metamask)\nLink: Add Monad Testnet (topic add-monad-testnet)\n\n[topic wallet-wont-load] Your wallet: The wallet part of the page doesn’t load.\nCheck your connection, then reload the page. Your favourites and email check stay.\nIf it still doesn’t load, a content blocker may be stopping it. Allow stridemon.xyz or try another browser.\n\n[topic wallet-not-answering] Your wallet: My wallet doesn’t answer.\nOpen MetaMask and make sure it’s unlocked. On a phone, switch to MetaMask, look for the request, then come back.\nStill nothing? Tap Use another wallet and connect again.\n\n[topic sign-in-failed] Your wallet: Signing in didn’t work.\nMaybe you said no in your wallet, the request ran out (it lasts 5 minutes), or the signature didn’t check out. Signing in again is free and sends nothing.\nIf it keeps failing, disconnect your wallet and connect it again, or try MetaMask.\n\n[topic wrong-network] Your wallet: My wallet won’t switch to Monad Testnet.\nAdd Monad Testnet by hand, then switch to it. The guide has a one-tap button and the details.\nOn the website you can sign in and mint without it. The app needs it.\nLink: Add Monad Testnet (topic add-monad-testnet)\n\n[topic minting-not-open] The mint: Minting hasn’t opened yet.\nThe schedule on the Founding Pass page shows when it opens. Meanwhile, heart the passes you like, and join the waitlist to mint 48 hours before everyone else.\nLink: See the Founding Passes (https://stridemon.xyz/pass)\n\n[topic waitlist-only] The mint: “Right now, only the waitlist can mint.”\nFor the first 48 hours, only emails that joined the waitlist before the window opened can mint. Joining now doesn’t get you in.\nAnyone can mint when the open mint starts. Add a reminder, and heart your favourites so they’re easy to find. Joined with another email? Check that one instead.\nLink: See the Founding Passes (https://stridemon.xyz/pass)\n\n[topic pass-taken] The mint: Someone minted the pass I wanted.\nEach pass exists once, and the first mint wins. Nothing was minted for you.\nYou see three similar passes nobody has yet. One tap mints one.\n\n[topic mint-slow] The mint: My mint is slow, or the page lost touch.\nMints go one after another, and yours is held for you in the queue. Nothing is lost.\nKeep the page open, or come back later in the same browser: the page picks your mint up again. Check your connection if it says it lost touch.\n\n[topic mint-failed] The mint: The mint didn’t go through.\nNothing was minted and nothing was charged, so you can try again. If it keeps happening, write to us.\nLink: Write to us (topic contact)\n\n[topic already-a-founder] The mint: It says I already have a pass.\nIt’s one pass per email and one per wallet. The page shows the pass you already hold.\nYour next step is the app: sign in with the wallet that holds it. Lost that wallet? Support can move your pass.\nLink: Sign in with the same wallet (topic sign-in-app)\nLink: Lost your wallet? (topic lost-wallet)\n\n[topic all-minted] The mint: All 1,000 are minted, or minting has closed.\nNo new passes, ever. StrideMon is open to everyone now: get the app and sign in for a free Sneaker.\nLink: Download the app (https://expo.dev/artifacts/eas/Aa0J7FXKPHyaKSGL-74nW66qSugLVcvhOMLyRrGL2iY.apk)\n\n[topic too-many-tries] The mint: “Too many tries.”\nToo many requests came from your connection in a short time. Wait a few minutes, then try again.\n\n[topic cant-reach-stridemon] The mint: “We can’t reach StrideMon” or “Something went wrong”.\nNothing was minted or lost. Check your connection and try again in a minute.\nIf it keeps happening, it’s probably on our side. Write to us, and say what you were doing.\nLink: Write to us (topic contact)\n\n[topic app-no-pass] The app: The app says “Mint a Founding Pass to get in early”.\nRight now, only founders can play. The app looks for a pass in the wallet you signed in with.\nMinted already? Check that the address the app shows is the wallet you minted with. If not, tap Sign out and sign in with that one.\nJust minted? Tap I’ve minted my pass. A new pass can take a few seconds to show.\nPlayed before early access? The game started over for the Founding Pass, so Sneakers and STRIDE from the test period don’t carry over.\nNo pass yet? Tap See the Founding Passes. The app opens to everyone when all 1,000 are minted, or on the last date in the schedule.\nLink: See the Founding Passes (https://stridemon.xyz/pass)\nLink: Sign in with the same wallet (topic sign-in-app)\n\n[topic app-cant-connect] The app: The app can’t connect my wallet.\nMost often, Monad Testnet isn’t turned on in MetaMask, so MetaMask shares no account.\n1. In MetaMask, add and turn on Monad Testnet.\n2. Clear the app’s data: Android Settings → Apps → StrideMon → Storage → Clear data.\n3. Open StrideMon and connect again.\nLink: Add Monad Testnet (topic add-monad-testnet)\n\n[topic app-wallet-stopped-answering] The app: Every wallet request fails in the app.\nThis happens when the app was closed while MetaMask was asking you something. Nothing reached Monad.\nGo to Profile, tap Sign out, then sign in again.\n\n[topic app-sign-in-expired] The app: “Your sign-in has expired.”\nGo to Profile, tap Sign out, then sign in again with the same wallet.\n\n[topic sneaker-not-arriving] The app: My Founder Sneaker, or my free Sneaker, isn’t arriving.\nIt usually takes a few seconds. If the app says it couldn’t request or mint it, tap Try again or Check again: nothing was charged.\nIf the app stays on that screen for more than a few minutes, write to us with your wallet address.\nLink: Write to us (topic contact)\n\n[topic app-cant-read-monad] The app: “Couldn’t read … from Monad.”\nThe app reads your pass and Sneaker straight from Monad Testnet, which is sometimes slow. Check your connection and tap Try again.\n\n[topic founder-sneaker-cant-send] The app: I can’t send my Founder Sneaker.\nFounder Sneakers stay with their founder: they can’t be sent or sold, like the pass. Normal Sneakers can be sent.\nLink: What “can’t be sent or sold” means (topic cant-be-sent-or-sold)\n\n[topic game-paused] The app: “StrideMon is paused for maintenance.”\nStarting a run, repairs and upgrades are off for a short while. Everything you own is safe, and anything waiting goes through by itself when the game is back.\n\n[topic lost-wallet] Lost your wallet?\nIf you lose the wallet that holds your pass (a lost phone and no Secret Recovery Phrase, say), support can move your pass and your Founder Sneaker to a new wallet. We do it by hand, and it’s the one way a pass ever moves.\nThey keep everything: the design, the founder number, the frame, laced or not, and the Sneaker’s level and stats.\n1. Make a new wallet. It can’t already hold a Founding Pass.\n2. Write to yashmittalmm@gmail.com from the email you minted with. Send your pass number (like #0137) and the new wallet’s address.\n3. We reply with a 6-digit code to that email. Send it back, so we know the email is yours.\n4. We move your pass and Founder Sneaker, usually within two days, and tell you when it’s done. Then sign in to the app with the new wallet.\nNever send your Secret Recovery Phrase or password. We’ll never ask for them.\n\n[topic contact] Contact\nWrite to us. A real person reads every email. Email: yashmittalmm@gmail.com.\nHelp us help you: include: what you were doing; the words on the screen, or a screenshot; your wallet address (it starts with 0x and is safe to share); your pass number, if you have one; your phone or browser.\nNever send your Secret Recovery Phrase or password. We’ll never ask for them.\nOr ask on X: @stridemon (https://x.com/stridemon)'
